Z||000007||FieroKyle||10-04-2001||10:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>Hey kyle,<BR>where did you find a drag strip out around GR?  I'd love to take mine to it sometime.  Boy, i'll bet the lexus was a nice kill.  "Kiss my a$$ my 2000 dollar car beat your 50,000 dollar ride"<P>btw, what's your 0-60?  I"m tryin to figure out why mine is sooo slow<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well in, our town, or atleast highschool it is known as "the strip" Its at Fallasburg PArk right on the same road Fierowrecker lives on. Hardly no cars. Also its rare for cops. Its Perfectly straight, perfectly flat, and it exactly 1/4 mile long from where the road begins to where this huge sweeping hill starts. (use the hill to slow down on) They had a guy time me, and a guy time the Stang' with stop watches. I had a 15.28, he had a 15.16. Alot of people have been killed and sh#t here from racing so it can be a touchy thing if ya ever got caught racing. Only drag strip that I know of in Michigan that I have looked at that attracts local guys is this strip up by the Edmore/Stanton area (60 miles outside of downtown GR). The Lexus was one of those smaller ones and had a bunch of punkass kids in it. Not one of the higher end of the models (guessitmation of $26,000 car) My 0 to 60 is like high 7's low 8's, depending on weather, and If I want to hear the engine crank 6000 rpms.<BR>Well for all the people that do live in the GR area, the Intrepid race was across from Amway on M-21, I raced him twice. The Malibu was on the East Beltline South of 28th street. If it was a drag race, I would have killed him, but since it was pretty much a passing gear race, it was a tie. The details of that as follows.<BR>I making a Michigan U-turn on the beltline and I was trying to catch this yellow light, so of course everybody at the red, 1 saw the car and my lisence plate TICKET (the plate seems to attract racers),lol, and could hear the car, 3 was burning rubber going through the corner making high pitched noises, just some, lol. Anyway, so this Malibu comes through traffic like a bat out of hell and lines up with me, both staying right beside eachother slow down to like 40 to 50, then he through his hand forward signalling to go and it was on. I got a car length on him right away, then he start clipping inches off every second till we hit about 100 to 110, then I started to gain for a second but had to let off do to slower traffic ahead, of course he didn't brake and flies ahead of me. I was sort of impressed though by the Malibu, really. So I catch back up to him, stick my hand out for a wave and then a thumbs up. He was a guy about 28, wasn't trying to look cool, just out having some fun. The Intrepid though had like 3 guys in it about 16 to 18, all smoking and ****  trying to look like punk asses with their stereo cranked. So I raced them and kicked their asses by alot, couple car lengths atleast.||||reg||1
